Windows CI: on the hosted runner's software adapter (WARP), a process that builds engine after
engine can still end partway through (row WARP-ACCUMULATION; 656 makes the local repro pass but
not the runner). Nearly every rustkit-engine lib test builds an engine, which draws with the GPU.

This patch adds one probe test, test_adapter_report, which prints the device type of the adapter
the engine's tests draw with. scripts/collect_metrics.py runs it first and, on a software adapter
("Cpu"), does not run the engine's lib tests (SOFTWARE_ADAPTER_SKIP, with the reason in the job
log and metrics.json). The full engine suite runs on a hardware GPU with every sync and its
receipt goes in the sync PR.

Remove when WARP-ACCUMULATION is fixed (or the runner gets a GPU).

diff --git a/crates/rustkit-engine/src/lib.rs b/crates/rustkit-engine/src/lib.rs
index 5f51c416..46e02ea3 100644
--- a/crates/rustkit-engine/src/lib.rs
+++ b/crates/rustkit-engine/src/lib.rs
@@ -65,6 +65,18 @@ pub(crate) fn test_compositor() -> Result<Compositor, rustkit_compositor::Compos
     Ok(shared.share_device())
 }
 
+/// The adapter the engine's tests draw with, as one line for the CI runner: on a software adapter
+/// `scripts/collect_metrics.py` does not run the engine's lib tests (see `SOFTWARE_ADAPTER_SKIP`
+/// there); the full suite runs on a hardware GPU with every sync.
+#[cfg(test)]
+#[test]
+fn test_adapter_report() {
+    match test_compositor() {
+        Ok(compositor) => println!("TEST ADAPTER: {:?}", compositor.adapter_info().device_type),
+        Err(e) => println!("TEST ADAPTER: none ({e})"),
+    }
+}
+
